man slumped over desk dead, with a pencil sticking out of his ear.  blood dripping out and pooling on the desk.  He has been dead for awhile, greyish skin - decomposing.  wearing a white button down shirt, no tie, sleeves rolled up to his forearm.  in one hand he has a feather quill, and there's an ink bottle tipped over with ink spilled onto the desk.  his eyeglasses are askew.  in his other hand he has a handwritten note "do not resuscitate".  he's slumped over an open book, the title can be seen.  the title is 'What ails you?'.  there is a computer screen flashing "There is no cure for what ails you."

There are a number of items on the desk.  a small globe, the top of the globe is flipped open on a hinge - the globe is actually an ashtray and it's overflowing with snuffed out cigarette butts.  blank sheet music paper - no notes are on the sheet music paper they're blank.  there is a trash can full of crumpled up sheet music with notes.  there is a telephone, off the hook, with the receiver hanging down toward the floor by the cord.

there is a credenza behind him with a small bookshelf and a chalkboard on the wall. there is a mouse or a rat, in a cage with a wheel - dead and desiccating.  there is an old style clock, within a glass dome but the clock is melting.  there is a goldfish in a bowl of dirty murky water, dead.  

